From 464e6f01ca52f6bc75b9e8bac6bda35c75a5b518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:58:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): validate foreign assignment originals
 canonically [daveey]

Assignment repair completion assumed its original task was in the executor's
local database. Portable repair execution can have split custody, causing a
valid repair to retry completion indefinitely.

Read a missing original and complete blocked history from the enrolled Board's
atomic execution-evidence endpoint before taking the writer lock. Bind the
short-lived observation to the repair key, refuse changed custody, and retain
capability/model and execution-authority validation. Never consult stale replica
rows or mutate the original. Scratch wire rows need no host-local path; other
workspace kinds refuse absent path evidence.

Proof: new foreign-original regression RED on base (5 failing, 11 passing),
GREEN with fix; eight affected suites passed 224 tests before additional race
controls; final custody/routing/model suites pass. scripts/check --base
origin/main passes. Read-only live canonical contract probe validates the exact
original assignment and one matching block without printing payloads.

Preliminary independent review found a local-materialization race; fixed by
refusing changed custody, with fresh/expired observation regressions. Final
exact-head review and required CI remain required before landing.
